---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Header from '../../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../../components/Footer.astro';
import Hero from '../../components/Hero.astro';
import ProcessSteps from '../../components/ProcessSteps.astro';
import { withBase } from '../../lib/paths';
import { localePath } from '../../lib/i18n';

const locale = 'en' as const;
---

<BaseLayout
  locale={locale}
  title="Method — Yardage"
  description="Analysis, data, production and print: the Yardage method for precise, consistent yardage books that reflect your club."
>
  <Header locale={locale} />
  <main>
    <Hero
      locale={locale}
      title="Method"
      subtitle="Four steps to turn the course into a reference book — precise, readable, and true to your club."
      image="/images/bg-fairway.jpg"
      compact
    />
    <ProcessSteps locale={locale} />

    <section class="border-b border-mist bg-paper">
      <div class="reveal mx-auto max-w-3xl px-5 py-16 md:px-8 md:py-20">
        <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-green-mid">01 — Analysis</p>
        <h2 class="mt-3 font-display text-2xl text-ink md:text-3xl">Understand the course before drawing it</h2>
        <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
          Every book starts with a careful reading of the land. We look at hole layouts, hazards, natural
          lines of play and the distances that actually matter to the player.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
          The goal is not to pile up measurements for their own sake, but to identify what helps build a
          strategy: where to play, where to avoid, where to aim. This step lays the foundation for a book
          that is useful on the course — not just aesthetic.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
          We also talk with the club. You know your course better than anyone — sensitive bunkers, risk
          areas, demanding greens. Your feedback sharpens our reading and ensures the book matches the
          reality of the land.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="border-b border-mist bg-sand">
      <div class="reveal mx-auto max-w-3xl px-5 py-16 md:px-8 md:py-20">
        <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-green-mid">02 — Data</p>
        <h2 class="mt-3 font-display text-2xl text-ink md:text-3xl">A reliable base, ready to evolve</h2>
        <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
          Once the course is analysed, we structure the information into a clear, consistent base.
          Distances, playing elements, cartographic landmarks: everything is organised to support book
          production.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
          This organisation has a concrete benefit for the club. When the course evolves — a new bunker,
          a renovated green, a redrawn fairway — the base can be updated without starting over. The book
          remains a living tool, not a frozen document.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
          For the player, that means reliable, consistent information from hole to hole. The same logic,
          the same landmarks, the same standard of care across the entire course.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="border-b border-mist bg-paper">
      <div class="reveal mx-auto max-w-3xl px-5 py-16 md:px-8 md:py-20">
        <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-green-mid">03 — Production</p>
        <h2 class="mt-3 font-display text-2xl text-ink md:text-3xl">Drawn to be read at a glance</h2>
        <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
          Production turns data into clear, hierarchical hole pages. Every element has its place:
          distances, hazards, lines of play, green. The player must be able to read the page quickly —
          on the tee or in the middle of the fairway.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
          We maintain strong consistency from hole to hole. A player discovering your course should find
          the same landmarks and the same logic of use across all eighteen holes. That is what makes a
          book a true standard — not a collection of isolated pages.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
          This shared structure still leaves room for the club’s identity. Cover, logo, partner mentions:
          the book remains yours, while being immediately recognisable as a Yardage book.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="border-b border-mist bg-sand">
      <div class="reveal mx-auto max-w-3xl px-5 py-16 md:px-8 md:py-20">
        <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-green-mid">04 — Print</p>
        <h2 class="mt-3 font-display text-2xl text-ink md:text-3xl">An object worthy of your pro shop</h2>
        <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
          The book is printed on eco-friendly paper, with finishes designed for course use and for
          presentation in the shop. It should feel good in the hand, hold up in the bag, and match the
          image you want to convey.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
          We handle printing and delivery to your club or pro shop. You do not need to coordinate a
          printer, formats or timelines: production is part of the method.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
          Result: a premium product, ready to offer to your members, visitors and competitors — with no
          technical burden on your side.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section-photo border-b border-mist">
      <img
        src={withBase('/images/bg-green.jpg')}
        alt=""
        class="section-photo-img"
        width="1280"
        height="1920"
        loading="lazy"
      />
      <div class="section-photo-veil"></div>
      <div class="mx-auto grid max-w-6xl gap-10 px-5 py-20 md:grid-cols-2 md:items-center md:px-8 md:py-28">
        <div class="reveal">
          <h2 class="font-display text-3xl text-ink md:text-4xl">What a hole page contains</h2>
          <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
            A Yardage page is built for decisions. It gathers the essential information without
            overwhelming the reader:
          </p>
          <ul class="mt-4 list-disc space-y-2 pl-5 text-base leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
            <li>useful distances to shape the shot;</li>
            <li>hazards and areas to anticipate;</li>
            <li>lines of play and course landmarks;</li>
            <li>green representation to prepare the approach and putting.</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
            Each hole is produced from course data for immediate reading on the ground. And because the
            base can be updated, the book can evolve with your club.
          </p>
          <div class="mt-8 flex flex-wrap gap-3">
            <a
              href={localePath(locale, 'contact')}
              class="inline-flex rounded-sm bg-white px-5 py-3 text-sm font-semibold text-brand transition hover:bg-ink"
            >
              Talk about your course
            </a>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="reveal reveal-delay-1 mx-auto w-full max-w-sm overflow-hidden border border-mist bg-panel">
          <img
            src={withBase('/images/exemple-trou-1.png')}
            alt="Yardage hole page example — hole 7, par 4"
            class="w-full"
            width="783"
            height="1378"
            loading="lazy"
          />
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="border-b border-mist bg-paper">
      <div class="reveal mx-auto max-w-3xl px-5 py-16 md:px-8 md:py-20">
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl text-ink md:text-3xl">
          A shared standard, an identity unique to each club
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
          Our method aims for a simple balance: a shared professional structure, and respect for the
          singularity of each course.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
          A player moving from one Yardage club to another should find the same landmarks and the same
          reading logic. That familiarity speeds up uptake and builds confidence during the round.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
          At the same time, each club keeps its history, architecture and image. The book is
          recognisable as a Yardage product — and as the official book of your club.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="border-b border-mist bg-sand">
      <div class="reveal mx-auto max-w-3xl px-5 py-16 md:px-8 md:py-20">
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl text-ink md:text-3xl">Ready to equip your course?</h2>
        <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
          From course analysis to book delivery, Yardage handles the full process. You keep control of
          the club’s identity; we ensure precision, consistency and product quality.
        </p>
        <div class="mt-10 flex flex-wrap gap-3">
          <a
            href={localePath(locale, 'contact')}
            class="inline-flex rounded-sm bg-brand px-5 py-3 text-sm font-semibold text-white transition hover:bg-ink"
          >
            Talk about your course
          </a>
          <a
            href={localePath(locale, 'offer')}
            class="inline-flex rounded-sm border border-mist px-5 py-3 text-sm font-semibold text-ink transition hover:bg-white/5"
          >
            View the offer
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
  <Footer locale={locale} />
</BaseLayout>
